# Follow-up to -16.play. That run's own `state` calls (already close to bare
# polling -- one per play/wait chunk) showed "You" dead with an unmoving
# "up in 6s"/"up in 7s" respawn readout (src/render/hud.ts:1548, the player's
# own respawn clock) across two screenshots 25 real/game seconds apart on The
# Three Cairns. "Tried and dropped" already closed a similar-looking report as
# a chained-play sampling artifact, but that retest used bare `wait`/`state`
# polling with no play() in between and found clean ~10s revivals every time.
# This repeats that exact bare-polling method on the same cell that just
# showed the stuck-looking shape, to tell an actual stall from another
# sampling coincidence.
open
tap battleground
tap map:conquest
tap class:druid:balance
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot t0

wait 5
state
shot t5

wait 5
state
shot t10

wait 5
state
shot t15

wait 5
state
shot t20

wait 5
state
shot t25

wait 5
state
shot t30
